# alias | mailbox address | display name
#
# alias            address the message was sent to. Exact, case-insensitive.
# mailbox address  that account's Mail address, not the SMTP login.
# display name     optional. Name only, not "Name <addr>".
#
# First match in the highest-priority header wins.
# Delivered-To, Envelope-To, X-Original-To, X-Envelope-To,
# X-Delivered-To, X-Rcpt-To, Original-Recipient, To, Cc, Bcc,
# Apparently-To, Resent-To, then Received "for <alias>".
# Within one header, file order wins.
#
# A mailbox column that does not match the compose account skips that alias.
# Set it. Otherwise a reply on another account can be rewritten too.
#
# Comments are whole lines. A pipe in the display name is fine (split is 3 fields).
# Plus-addresses are not folded: list sales+x@example.com itself if you need it.
#
# The SMTP login is not changed. The server has to allow this From
# (Gmail: Send mail as).
#
# Debug switch. Next reply picks it up, no restart.
# debug
# debug=on
# One session only: CLAWS_REPLYFROMALIAS_DEBUG=1 claws-mail
#
# sales@example.com | me@example.com | Example Sales
# jobs@example.com | me@example.com | Example Jobs
